as made. The position of the building, at the edge of the Eastern Roman Empire, prompts us to explore the cultural relations of this region with other parts of the empire and to examine its local context, in the cradle of the Syriac world.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
